# CPU Viz — Cursor Rules

Before implementing any feature:

1. Read [PROJECT_STATUS.md](../../PROJECT_STATUS.md) for current task
2. Read [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md) for structure and schema
3. Read [PRD.md](../../PRD.md) for feature requirements
4. Follow [cursor-rules.md](../../cursor-rules.md) workflow (explain → design → plan → implement → verify → update status)

## Stack

Next.js App Router · TypeScript · TailwindCSS · React Flow · D3.js · Framer Motion · PostgreSQL · Prisma

## Key Rules

- Server Components for data fetching; `"use client"` only when needed
- Visualization components are schema-driven via `config` props
- No hardcoded lesson/company data in components — use DB/seed
- Dynamic import viz libraries with `ssr: false`
- Update PROJECT_STATUS.md after completing tasks
- Minimize scope; no drive-by refactors
